<title>DUBAI: Saudi airline leases Boeings to carry pilgrims.</title>
<headline>Saudi airline leases Boeings to carry pilgrims.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabian Airlines Corp said on Tuesday it had leased nine Boeing 747 airplanes to help with its Moslem haj pilgrimage operations next month, the official Saudi Press Agency (SPA) said.</p>
<p>It quoted the airline's director-general, Khaled Ben-Bakr, as saying the jumbo jets would assist in the operation that will ensure the transportation some 204,000 pilgrims on 566 charter flights as well as 63,000 pilgrims on scheduled flights.</p>
<p>About two million Moslems -- half of them from abroad -- are expected to perform the annual haj in the kingdom, site of Islam's two holiest shrines.</p>
</text>
